ou and others downvote. it registers in your tags. then i remove my vote. presto! you''re the only one keeping it here!", "put in brackets", "hollywood hits", "new generations", "new generations philip glass", "compilatie", "celtic celebration", "leaving on a jet plan", "bflaminio", "ronak bhatt", "special purpose", "alabama thunderpussy", "dfree843", "cdnnnow128", "tag spam", "va - we were first - 180 hits in their original versions (2014)", "boot land", "s.a. souvenirs", "mugwart was a sludge/punk/doom/hardcore band from virginia beach", "active 1998\u20132002. emerging from the tidewater crust\u2011punk/skate scene", "the group combined punk urgency and hardcore aggression with downtuned sludge heaviness and doom atmosphere. their raw", "abrasive sound placed them firmly within the late\u20111990s/early\u20112000s underground", "while maintaining a distinctly punk ethos. the band\u2019s definitive release is discography (this dark reign recordings", "tdr\u201113", "usa)", "which compiles studio material from 1999\u20132002. tracks were originally issued (or intended) across several small\u2011label documents: \u201cbefore you / fallen\u201d \u2014 acrude records (crude\u201101", "france)", "7\u2033 single. because sometimes two are better than one \u2014 split with fistula", "shifty records (sh09", "3\u2033 cd. south of hell \u2013 14 songs from the new south \u2014 berserker records (ber\u2011005", "compilation. crushers killers destroyers! \u2014 shifty records (sh08", "compilation. doomed \u2014 this dark reign recordings (tdr\u2011001", "compilation. mugwart performed throughout virginia and the surrounding region", "sharing stages with grief", "damad", "fistula", "sofa king killer", "and clutch. in 2011", "uk extreme\u2011metal band dragged into sunlight selected mugwart\u2019s track \u201cfallen\u201d for a curated mixtape in terrorizer magazine (issue #285)", "highlighting the group\u2019s ongoing resonance nearly a decade after disbanding. legacy: though short\u2011lived", "mugwart is regarded as a cult", "foundational act of the virginia sludge/punk/doom underground. their recordings circulate digitally via bandcamp and streaming platforms", "and their influence continues to be cited by later generations of extreme bands. disambiguation: this is mugwart (virginia beach", "mugwart (has nothing to do with (\u201cmugwort\u201d)", "needs to be removed", "sludge hardcore punk", "ansage", "country dreams"]', 'A compilation album comprises tracks, which may be previously released or unreleased, usually from several separate recordings by either one performer or by several performers. If the recordings are from one artist, then generally the tracks were not originally intended for release together as a single work, but may be collected together as a greatest hits album or box set. If the recordings are from several artists, there may be a theme, topic, time period, or genre which links the tracks, or t', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Various_Artists', '2026-05-23 16:36:23', 2, 'Various Artists', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "artist_enrichment" VALUES('Eddie Kendricks', 'cf3ea6e9-c856-4737-a988-6b64cc9f2bf2', 'US', 1939, '[]', '["soul", "motown", "rock and indie"]', 'Edward James Kendrick (December 17, 1939 – October 5, 1992), better known as Eddie Kendricks, was an American tenor singer and songwriter. Noted for his distinctive falsetto singing style, Kendricks co-founded the Motown singing group the Temptations, and was one of their lead singers from 1961 until 1971. He was the lead voice on such famous songs as "The Way You Do the Things You Do", "Get Ready", and "Just My Imagination (Running Away with Me)".  As a solo artist, Kendricks recorded several h', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eddie_Kendricks', '2026-05-23 23:45:14', 6, 'Eddie Kendricks', '["soul", "funk", "motown", "Disco", "rnb"]', 'Eddie Kendricks (Edward James Kendrick, Union Springs, Alabama, December 17, 1939 – Birmingham, Alabama, October 5, 1992), was an American singer and songwriter, noted for his distinctive falsetto singing style. Kendricks co-founded the Motown singing group The Temptations, and was one of their lead singers from 1960 until 1971. His was the lead voice on such famous songs as "The Way You Do The Things You Do", "Get Ready", and "Just My Imagination".', '291396', '1618025', 'https://www.last.fm/music/Eddie+Kendricks');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "artist_enrichment" VALUES('The Pacific Cowboys', 'bd872e2f-3dce-4932-b8dc-91cf949cfbb5', 'FI', 1986, '[]', '["rock", "hard rock", "folk rock", "comedy rock", "novelty"]', 'The Leningrad Cowboys (also known as LC Cowboys) are a Finnish rock band who perform rock and roll covers of other songs as well as original material. They have exaggerated pompadour hairstyles and wore long pointy shoes.  They often worked with the Russian military band the Alexandrov Ensemble.', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leningrad_Cowboys', '2026-05-23 16:36:36', 1, 'Leningrad Cowboys', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
