ime you and others downvote. it registers in your tags. then i remove my vote. presto! you''re the only one keeping it here!", "put in brackets", "hollywood hits", "new generations", "new generations philip glass", "compilatie", "celtic celebration", "leaving on a jet plan", "bflaminio", "ronak bhatt", "special purpose", "alabama thunderpussy", "dfree843", "cdnnnow128", "tag spam", "va - we were first - 180 hits in their original versions (2014)", "boot land", "s.a. souvenirs", "mugwart was a sludge/punk/doom/hardcore band from virginia beach", "active 1998\u20132002. emerging from the tidewater crust\u2011punk/skate scene", "the group combined punk urgency and hardcore aggression with downtuned sludge heaviness and doom atmosphere. their raw", "abrasive sound placed them firmly within the late\u20111990s/early\u20112000s underground", "while maintaining a distinctly punk ethos. the band\u2019s definitive release is discography (this dark reign recordings", "tdr\u201113", "usa)", "which compiles studio material from 1999\u20132002. tracks were originally issued (or intended) across several small\u2011label documents: \u201cbefore you / fallen\u201d \u2014 acrude records (crude\u201101", "france)", "7\u2033 single. because sometimes two are better than one \u2014 split with fistula", "shifty records (sh09", "3\u2033 cd. south of hell \u2013 14 songs from the new south \u2014 berserker records (ber\u2011005", "compilation. crushers killers destroyers! \u2014 shifty records (sh08", "compilation. doomed \u2014 this dark reign recordings (tdr\u2011001", "compilation. mugwart performed throughout virginia and the surrounding region", "sharing stages with grief", "damad", "fistula", "sofa king killer", "and clutch. in 2011", "uk extreme\u2011metal band dragged into sunlight selected mugwart\u2019s track \u201cfallen\u201d for a curated mixtape in terrorizer magazine (issue #285)", "highlighting the group\u2019s ongoing resonance nearly a decade after disbanding. legacy: though short\u2011lived", "mugwart is regarded as a cult", "foundational act of the virginia sludge/punk/doom underground. their recordings circulate digitally via bandcamp and streaming platforms", "and their influence continues to be cited by later generations of extreme bands. disambiguation: this is mugwart (virginia beach", "mugwart (has nothing to do with (\u201cmugwort\u201d)", "needs to be removed", "sludge hardcore punk", "ansage", "country dreams"]', 'A compilation album comprises tracks, which may be previously released or unreleased, usually from several separate recordings by either one performer or by several performers. If the recordings are from one artist, then generally the tracks were not originally intended for release together as a single work, but may be collected together as a greatest hits album or box set. If the recordings are from several artists, there may be a theme, topic, time period, or genre which links the tracks, or t', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Various_Artists', '2026-05-23 16:38:09', 1, 'Various Artists', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "artist_enrichment" VALUES('Iggy Pop & James Williamson', 'f37b3f31-b1f8-4b88-8cb5-b34f709b17d7', 'US', 1947, '[]', '["rock", "alternative rock", "punk", "american", "punk rock", "post-punk", "new wave", "hard rock", "usa", "glam rock", "art rock", "classic rock", "garage rock", "protopunk", "shock rock", "proto punk", "classic pop and rock", "proto-punk", "singers", "actors", "guitarists", "2008 universal fire victim", "punk rock musicians"]', 'James Newell Osterberg Jr. (born April 21, 1947), known professionally as Iggy Pop, is an American singer, songwriter, musician, and actor who was the lead vocalist of the proto-punk band the Stooges. Regarded as the "Godfather of Punk", he is noted for his outrageous and unpredictable stage antics, poetic lyrics, and unique voice. He was named one of the 50 Great Voices by NPR, inducted into the Rock and Roll Hall of Fame as a member of the Stooges in 2010, and received a Grammy Lifetime Achiev', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iggy_Pop', '2026-05-23 16:38:10', 20, 'Iggy Pop', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "artist_enrichment" VALUES('Sachet', '9d1f8ef5-1c40-41ce-8d5a-2768df2f5644', NULL, 2016, '[]', '["indie rock"]', 'Although its most usual definition is that listed under "packet" (see link above), a sachet ( sash-ay) can also mean a small scented cloth bag filled with herbs, potpourri, or aromatic ingredients; or a small porous bag or packet containing a material intended to interact with its atmosphere;  for example, desiccants are usually packed in sachets which are then placed in larger packages. Cotton, linen or organza are used to create the bag.', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sachet', '2026-05-23 23:52:57', 18, 'Sachet', '["power pop", "pop", "indie rock", "punk rock", "argentina 80"]', NULL, '1161', '7019', 'https://www.last.fm/music/sachet');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "artist_enrichment" VALUES('Prince Jammy and Scientist', '7d2f071d-ffa4-4ce7-bea2-0685374c1b2a', 'JM', 1947, '[]', '["reggae", "dub", "producer", "ragga"]', 'Lloyd Woodrowe James  (born 26 October 1947), better known as Prince Jammy or King Jammy, is a Jamaican dub mixer, sound system owner and record producer. He began his musical career as a dub master at King Tubby''s recording studio. His dubs are known for their clear sound and use of effects.', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prince_Jammy', '2026-05-23 16:38:24', 1, 'Prince Jammy', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "artist_enrichment" VALUES('Rangers & Kim Fowley', '6bedf676-3e23-46ef-a008-720ded2b9a06', 'US', 1939, '[]', '["rock", "psychedelic rock", "garage rock"]', 'Kim Vincent Fowley (July 21, 1939 – January 15, 2015) was an American record producer, songwriter, and musician who was behind a string of novelty and cult pop rock singles in the 1960s, and managed the Runaways in the 1970s. He has been described as "one of the most colorful characters in the annals of rock & roll", as well as "a shadowy cult figure well outside the margins of the mainstream".', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kim_Fowley', '2026-05-23 16:38:32', 1, 'Kim Fowley', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "artist_enrichment" VALUES('Prison Affair', '85d53d76-8191-42b8-8512-88267cffa694', 'ES', NULL, '[]', '["punk"]', NULL, NULL, '2026-05-23 23:45:32', 11, 'Prison Affair', '["egg punk", "synthpunk", "Garage Punk", "post-punk", "Garage Rock"]', 'Egg punk band from Barcelona, Spain.', '86121', '1319692', 'https://www.last.fm/music/Prison+Affair');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "artist_enrichment" VALUES('Miss Destiny', '2572151f-6984-4856-9b0d-c8855f343087', 'DE', NULL, '[]', '[]', NULL, NULL, '2026-05-23 23:45:32', 4, 'Miss Destiny', '["trance", "dance", "House", "electronic", "hands up"]', 'There are at least two artists with this name:  1) Destiny was born in a little town in the North of Germany . She discovered her love for Dance Music  and singing in the early 90´s. At the age of 12 she started to write own songs together with her best friends.  Purely by chance she met the producers Tunebazz inc. and Daydream in 2006 and finally she decided to borrow her voice for some of their tracks. Shaun Bate took notice of her voice and asked her for a collaboration.', '13119', '71006', 'https://www.last.fm/music/Miss+Destiny');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "artist_enrichment" VALUES('Lithics', 'c98690bd-7a66-4104-89e6-46a6237ee1fc', 'US', NULL, '[]', '["experimental", "punk"]', NULL, NULL, '2026-05-23 23:45:33', 26, 'Lithics', '["post-punk", "Crank wave", "art punk", "experimental", "good"]', 'This is music in ellipses. A circular communication and a fusion of decades worth of musical insight into a singular refraction of thought & sound. Guitars plunk and scratch, and rhythms pulse and syncopate tightly wound around an imagist''s philosophy to "use absolutely no word that does not contribute to the presentation." The band''s austere approach to composition and wordplay elevates them above and beyond bands seeking similar sounds; it''s not that they use less; it''s HOW they use less.', '30350', '294138', 'https://www.last.fm/music/Lithics');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "artist_enrichment" VALUES('The Galaxies', 'd47e2de0-4a06-45cf-a097-7dbabeed9c79', NULL, NULL, '[]', '[]', NULL, NULL, '2026-05-23 23:45:33', 2, 'The Galaxies', '["All", "rock", "power pop", "Garage Rock", "brazilian"]', '1) Brazilian group from the sixities. Only one album relased on 1968, considered the one  history band of the brazilian psychedelic era.  2) The Galaxies, a Northwest rock band, was founded in the 1960s in Tacoma, Washington, at Stadium High School. The first rock band to ever play for a dance in Stadium High School, The Galaxies became one of the house bands at the Red Carpet Teenage Nightclub in Tacoma, and went on to record for Etiquette Records and Jerden Records. The Galaxies performed throughout the Northwest from 1962 until 1968.', '3334', '22641', 'https://www.last.fm/music/The+Galaxies');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "artist_enrichment" VALUES('Bosna', '8d52db99-0e9c-49ac-8d2e-851ea158e353', 'IT', NULL, '[]', '["cellist"]', NULL, NULL, '2026-05-23 16:38:38', 3, 'Pietro Bosna', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "artist_enrichment" VALUES('The Firesign Theatre', 'ed79f6c9-a484-46d7-acd6-241444f26d8a', 'US', 1966, '[]', '["comedy", "radio", "al", "audio drama", "sketch comedy"]', NULL, NULL, '2026-05-23 23:45:34', 1, 'The Firesign Theatre', '["comedy", "satire", "humour", "psychedelic", "podcast"]', 'A comedy troupe consisting of Phil Austin, Peter Bergman, David Ossman, and Philip Proctor, The Firesign Theatre have been creating "weirdly cool" recordings since the mid-1960s.  Fans of old radio will love their rich, hallucinatory environments, dripping with satire and filled with cultural references revealing themselves to the perceptive listener.  In 2005, the classic album Don''t Crush That Dwarf, Hand Me The Pliers was selected to be preserved in the US National Recording Registry.', '9169', '120768', 'https://www.last.fm/music/The+Firesign+Theatre');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "artist_enrichment" VALUES('Ivan', '6640d654-4b8f-48ed-883c-e064a0a48861', 'IT', 1945, '[]', '["singer-songwriter", "pop rock", "rock"]', NULL, NULL, '2026-05-23 16:38:46', 7, 'Ivan Graziani', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "artist_enrichment" VALUES('Vintage Crop', '00c21d63-04d0-49d7-ae8e-d27b1754c17a', 'AU', 2012, '[]', '[]', 'Vintage Crop (1 March 1987 – 14 July 2014) was a British-bred Irish-trained Thoroughbred racehorse best known for becoming the first northern hemisphere trained runner to win Australia''s premier race the Melbourne Cup. The chestnut gelding competed in flat racing in Ireland, England, and Australia from 1992 to 1995.  He won 16 races in Ireland, England, and Australia.  For his performance during the 1993 racing season he earned the Cartier Award for Top Stayer.', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vintage_Crop', '2026-05-23 23:45:35', 13, 'Vintage Crop', '["punk", "Garage Rock", "hardcore", "punk rock", "melbourne"]', 'Australian band from Geelong, consisting of Jack Cherry, Tyson Harper, Jack Massey and Tyler O''Brien. Obviously, anti-capitalistic sentiment has a long history in punk, dating back to the Dead Kennedys and Rudimentary Peni; this spirit lives on vibrantly in Vintage Crop, a four-piece hailing from Geelong, Australia. The group might not believe in the old nine-to-five, but they do believe in noise—and to that end, they’re undeniably good at what they do here.   Facebook Bandcamp', '9346', '103395', 'https://www.last.fm/music/Vintage+Crop');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "artist_enrichment" VALUES('Scorpions', 'c3cceeed-3332-4cf0-8c4c-bbde425147b6', 'DE', 1965, '[]', '["rock", "progressive rock", "70s", "hairmetal", "80s", "heavy metal", "krautrock", "german", "metal", "hard rock", "power metal", "classic rock", "acoustic rock", "pop rock", "glam metal", "european", "aor", "80''s", "70''s", "loriel", "aln-sh", "alemanha"]', NULL, NULL, '2026-05-23 23:45:36', 9, 'Scorpions', '["hard rock", "classic rock", "heavy metal", "rock", "80s"]', 'Scorpions are a German hard rock band formed in Hanover in 1965 by guitarist Rudolf Schenker. The longest-running line-up of the band, active from 1978 to 1992, included Schenker, Klaus Meine on vocals, Matthias Jabs on lead guitar, Francis Buchholz on bass, and Herman Rarebell on drums. Schenker has been the only continuous member, while Meine has been with the band since 1969, Jabs since 1978, and bassist Paweł Mąciwoda and drummer Mikkey Dee joined in 2003 and 2016, respectively.', '2870424', '89206837', 'https://www.last.fm/music/Scorpions');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "artist_enrichment" VALUES('Clash', '8f92558c-2baa-4758-8c38-615519e9deda', 'GB', 1976, '[]', '["rock", "punk", "punk rock", "british", "post-punk", "new wave", "uk", "funk", "reggae rock", "english", "dance-punk", "england", "classic pop and rock", "server name", "reino unido"]', NULL, NULL, '2026-05-23 16:38:49', 8, 'The Clash', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "artist_enrichment" VALUES('Kraftwerk', '5700dcd4-c139-4f31-aa3e-6382b9af9032', 'DE', 1970, '[]', '["rock", "electronic", "synthpop", "industrial", "krautrock", "german", "electro", "techno", "synth-pop", "neue deutsche welle", "electronic music", "european", "synth pop", "progressive electronic", "classic pop and rock", "ndw"]', NULL, NULL, '2026-05-23 23:45:37', 48, 'Kraftwerk', '["electronic", "synthpop", "german", "electronica", "krautrock"]', 'Kraftwerk ("power plant" in English) are an electronic band founded in 1970 in Düsseldorf, Germany. They pioneered electronic music in the 70s and are considered the most important and influential band of their genre, often described as "the godfathers of electronic music". Kraftwerk''s sound is minimalistic and strictly electronic; it combines driving, repetitive rhythms with catchy melodies and vocals usually sung through a vocoder. The current line-up consists of Ralf Hütter (the only original member)', '1402976', '42455963', 'https://www.last.fm/music/Kraftwerk');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "artist_enrichment" VALUES('Klaus Schulze', '2e710b0c-6ff3-4c21-87d5-16ebbbca212c', 'DE', 1947, '[]', '["rock", "trance", "electronic", "progressive rock", "krautrock", "ambient", "germany", "german", "new age", "space", "european", "progressive electronic", "berlin school", "space music", "space ambient", "kosmische musik"]', NULL, NULL, '2026-05-23 23:45:38', 5, 'Klaus Schulze', '["electronic", "ambient", "krautrock", "experimental", "berlin school"]', 'Klaus Schulze (4 August 1947 – 26 April 2022) was a German electronic music pioneer, composer and musician who also used the alias Richard Wahnfried. He was briefly a member of the electronic band Tangerine Dream as well as co-founding Ash Ra Tempel before a pioneering and prolific solo career of 60+ albums (totalling 110+ CDs) across six decades.  In 1969, Klaus Schulze was the drummer of one of the early incarnations of Tangerine Dream for their debut album Electronic Meditation.', '199859', '3223374', 'https://www.last.fm/music/Klaus+Schulze');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "artist_enrichment" VALUES('David Essex', '822e180a-061a-4da0-a1f3-35e8bdf5f240', 'GB', 1947, '[]', '["rock", "british", "soft rock", "uk", "english"]', NULL, NULL, '2026-05-23 23:45:38', 4, 'David Essex', '["pop", "70s", "rock", "glam rock", "male vocalists"]', 'David Essex OBE (born David Albert Cook, 23 July 1947) is an English singer-songwriter and actor who rose to fame in the 1970s. He achieved 19 UK Top 40 singles—including two number ones—and 16 Top 40 albums between 1973 and 1994. Internationally, he is best known for his 1973 hit "Rock On", which reached No. 5 in the US and earned a Grammy nomination.  Born in Plaistow, East London, Essex initially pursued football and played for West Ham United Juniors before turning to music.', '211193', '1149025', 'https://www.last.fm/music/David+Essex');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "artist_enrichment" VALUES('The Duvals', '4d7ef3bf-7a86-46b6-9bc2-446f72568ae9', NULL, NULL, '[]', '[]', NULL, NULL, '2026-05-23 23:45:39', 1, 'The Duvals', '["oldies", "punk rock", "melodic", "melodic punk", "doo wop"]', 'The Duvals are a two-man electro rock band from Paris, FR.', '373', '1700', 'https://www.last.fm/music/The+Duvals');
