INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "artist_enrichment" VALUES('Neutrals', '6e521d26-1d86-4d74-b35c-6ca4e3cbaf46', NULL, NULL, '[]', '["post-punk"]', NULL, NULL, '2026-05-23 23:50:54', 2, 'Neutrals', '["indie rock", "USA", "post-punk"]', 'Neutrals are Allan McNaughton (Giant Haystacks, Airfix Kits) on guitar and vocals, Phil Benson (Terry Malts, Magic Bullets) on bass and vocals, and Phil Lantz (Cocktails, Razz, Airfix Kits) on drums. The group channels a wide range of 70s and 80s punk, post-punk, and indie pop influences. They live in the San Francisco Bay Area.', '4360', '40700', 'https://www.last.fm/music/NEUTRALS');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "artist_enrichment" VALUES('Billy Lee Riley & His Little Green Men', '8f8b91b8-3a78-41b1-941e-60137b72aefe', NULL, NULL, '[]', '[]', NULL, NULL, '2026-05-23 16:59:37', 1, 'Billy Lee Riley and His Little Green Men', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "artist_enrichment" VALUES('Little Eva', '531643e6-b3ba-4c7f-9d0d-f2831dc42317', 'US', 1943, '[]', '["girl group", "rhythm & blues", "brill building"]', NULL, NULL, '2026-05-23 23:50:55', 5, 'Little Eva', '["60s", "soul", "oldies", "pop", "female vocalists"]', 'Eva Narcissus Boyd (June 29, 1943 – April 10, 2003), known by the stage name of Little Eva, was an American pop singer.  Born in Belhaven, North Carolina, she moved to the Brighton Beach section of Brooklyn, New York, at a young age.  Although some sources claim that her stage name was inspired by a character from the novel Uncle Tom''s Cabin, she stated in an interview that she was named after her aunt, which prompted her family to call her "Little Eva.', '298620', '1291500', 'https://www.last.fm/music/Little+Eva');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "artist_enrichment" VALUES('School Damage', 'e4f66ea2-cb01-416a-9907-e4d338959a29', 'AU', 2015, '[]', '[]', NULL, NULL, '2026-05-23 23:50:55', 20, 'School Damage', '["australia", "canada", "punk rock"]', 'There are at least 2 bands with this name:  1) Toronto, ON Punk Rock  Brad Manners- Guitar/Vox Jon Cabatan- Bass/Vox Curtis Tone- Drums/Muscles  School Damage’s gritty but melodic style of punk rock is a mix of raw hardcore energy and Ramones- four chords worship. The songs start and stop on a dime while dripping enough piss and vinegar to leave you dehydrated and thirsty for more.   After four years, three drummers, many kilometers and a handful of releases', '4031', '46710', 'https://www.last.fm/music/School+Damage');
