INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "artist_enrichment" VALUES('Shapes', '626be99f-0f07-4a10-9506-7721d3d37a8e', 'GB', NULL, '[]', '[]', NULL, NULL, '2026-05-23 23:58:38', 2, 'Shapes', '["math rock", "post-hardcore", "Progressive rock", "experimental", "Progressive"]', 'There is more than one artist called Shapes:  1. SHAPES are a 3 piece math-rock/post-hardcore band from Birmingham, UK. They released their debut EP Get Your Learn On in 2008 with Godmonkey Recordings then signed to Big Scary Monsters to release  The Pasture, The Oil in 2009 and  Monotony Chic in 2011.  2. Shapes (UK) are a four piece Indie band hailing from Luton. Since their first gig back in April 2007, Jamie mack (Vocals), Matt Rushton (Guitar)', '60022', '295298', 'https://www.last.fm/music/Shapes');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "artist_enrichment" VALUES('The Need', 'd569b477-55e7-4487-8a26-dda5a6ddf3c8', 'US', 1996, '[]', '["queercore"]', NULL, NULL, '2026-05-23 23:58:38', 2, 'The Need', '["queercore", "experimental", "queer", "riot grrrl", "all-girl"]', 'There are at least three artists called The Need.    1. Started in the late 1990s, and broke up in 2000 formed by Rachel Carns and Radio Sloan as a "queercore band".  2. Originated in Brisbane, Australia by Bradley Stokes, Pharos Roche, and Steven Leslie in March, 2012.  (Alternative Rock)  3. THE NEED is a South Korean producer who has been creating music across various genres—hip-hop, R&B, pop, and electronic music—since 2018.  He is well known for working with some of Korea’s top artists and rappers, including BIBI, ATEEZ, I.', '9270', '71070', 'https://www.last.fm/music/The+Need');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "artist_enrichment" VALUES('The Cool Greenhouse', 'e3d22d9c-c6df-40e7-888b-67e8d2d9e759', 'GB', NULL, '[]', '["post-punk 2k"]', NULL, NULL, '2026-05-23 23:58:39', 18, 'The Cool Greenhouse', '["post-punk", "Crank wave", "art punk", "spoken word", "post-brexit new wave"]', 'Formed in rural Norfolk and fronted by spoken word artist Tom Greenhouse, the group deliver the type of post-punk lyrical realism that South London absolutely lusts after, effortlessly gliding through poignant observations on politics, the mundanity of living and pop culture gone wrong. Although joining a music scene that is already crowded with half-sung, half-spoken lyricists, The Cool Greenhouse have veered towards minimalism for an avant-garde slant that is frankly a refreshing deviation.', '35281', '344620', 'https://www.last.fm/music/The+Cool+Greenhouse');
